The HashMap Class Methods,`equals()` method,"Create two `HashMaps` with the same key-value pairs and verify they are equal using the `equals()` method."
The HashMap Class Methods,`equals()` with different Map types,"Check if a `HashMap` is `equals()` to a `TreeMap` containing the same key-value pairs."
The HashMap Class Methods,`get()` with a non-existent key,"Demonstrate that `get()` returns `null` when the key is not found in the map."
The HashMap Class Methods,`getOrDefault` with a method call,"Use a method call as the default value in `getOrDefault`, and show that the method is only called if the key is not present."
The HashMap Class Methods,`hashCode()` method,"Create two identical `HashMaps` and verify that their `hashCode()` values are the same."
The HashMap Class Methods,`keySet().contains()` vs `containsKey()`,"Compare the performance (conceptually) and usage of `map.keySet().contains(key)` versus `map.containsKey(key)`."
The HashMap Class Methods,`keySet()` Removal,"Remove an element from the `keySet()` and verify it is also removed from the original `HashMap`."
The HashMap Class Methods,`keySet()` View,"Modify the `HashMap` (e.g., by removing a key) and show that the change is reflected in the `Set` previously returned by `keySet()`."
The HashMap Class Methods,`merge` for frequency counting,"Re-implement the word frequency counter using the `merge()` method for a more concise solution."
The HashMap Class Methods,`merge` with null value,"Demonstrate how the `merge` function behaves when the existing value in the map is `null`."
The HashMap Class Methods,`put()` Return Value,"Call `put()` for a new key and for an existing key. Observe the return value in each case (it returns the old value, or null)."
The HashMap Class Methods,`putAll(Map m)`,"Create two `HashMaps` and use `putAll()` to copy all mappings from the second map into the first."
The HashMap Class Methods,`putAll` with overwriting,"Demonstrate that `putAll` will overwrite values in the destination map if the source map contains the same keys."
The HashMap Class Methods,`putIfAbsent` return value,"Demonstrate that `putIfAbsent` returns the current value (if present) or `null` (if the put succeeded)."
The HashMap Class Methods,`remove()` Return Value,"Call `remove()` for an existing key and a non-existent key. Observe the value returned in each case."
