The String Class,"ToUpperCase","Convert an entire String to uppercase using '.toUpperCase()'."
The String Class,"TrimWhitespace","Remove leading and trailing whitespace from a String using '.trim()'."
The String Class,Case Conversion,"Convert a string to all uppercase and all lowercase using 'toUpperCase()' and 'toLowerCase()'."
The String Class,Character Access,"Get and print the character at a specific index in a string using 'charAt()'."
The String Class,Checking for Empty or Blank,"(Java 11+) Use 'isEmpty()' and 'isBlank()' to check if a string is empty or contains only whitespace."
The String Class,Immutability,"Demonstrate the immutability of strings by showing that methods like 'concat()' or 'toUpperCase()' return a new string rather than modifying the original."
The String Class,Replacing Characters,"Use the 'replace()' method to replace all occurrences of a character or substring within a string."
The String Class,Searching in a String,"Use 'indexOf()' and 'startsWith()' to find the position of a character or substring and to check if a string begins with a certain prefix."
The String Class,Splitting a String,"Split a comma-separated string into an array of strings using the 'split()' method."
The String Class,String Comparison,"Compare two strings for equality using both '==' and the '.equals()' method. Explain the difference."
The String Class,String Formatting,"Use the 'String.format()' method to create a formatted string with placeholders for variables."
The String Class,String Length and Concatenation,"Create two strings, find their lengths, and concatenate them to form a new string."
The String Class,Substring,"Extract and print a substring from a given string using the 'substring()' method."
The String Class,Trimming Whitespace,"Use the 'trim()' method to remove leading and trailing whitespace from a string."
The System Class Methods,Application of arraycopy() - Array Expansion,"Write a method that uses `System.arraycopy()` to create a new, larger array and copy the elements of an old array into it."
The System Class Methods,Application of currentTimeMillis() - Timestamping,"Use `System.currentTimeMillis()` to create a unique, timestamp-based filename."
The System Class Methods,Application of exit() - Error Condition,"Write a program that validates user input and calls `System.exit(1)` if the input is invalid."
The System Class Methods,Application of getProperty() - OS Detection,"Use `System.getProperty("os.name")` to detect the underlying operating system and print a different message for Windows vs. Linux."
The System Class Methods,Application of getProperty() - User Home,"Use `System.getProperty("user.home")` to find the path to the current user's home directory."
The System Class Methods,Application of getenv() - Configuration,"Read a database connection string from an environment variable named `DB_CONNECTION_STRING`."
The System Class Methods,Application of nanoTime() - Benchmarking,"Use `System.nanoTime()` before and after a loop to measure how long it takes to execute."
The System Class Methods,Checking for a property's existence,"How can you check if a system property is set without providing a default? (Hint: check for `null`)."
The System Class Methods,Combining `getProperty` and `lineSeparator`,"Construct a multi-line string showing the Java version and OS name, separated by the system's line separator."
The System Class Methods,Combining `user.home` and `file.separator`,"Construct a full, platform-independent path to a file named `config.txt` inside the user's home directory."
The System Class Methods,Comparing `getenv` and `getProperty`,"Print a property that exists as both (e.g., `user.name` vs `USER`). Discuss the difference in their sources."
The System Class Methods,Default properties,"Name three system properties that are guaranteed to be available in any Java environment."
The System Class Methods,Environment variable case sensitivity,"Check if `System.getenv()` is case-sensitive on your OS by trying to get a variable with different casings (e.g., `PATH` vs `path`)."
The System Class Methods,Field - err,"Use `System.err.println()` to print an error message to the standard error stream."
The System Class Methods,Field - in,"Use `System.in` as the source for a `Scanner` to read user input from the console."
The System Class Methods,Field - out,"Use `System.out.println()` to print the classic ""Hello
The System Class Methods,Final Project - App Configuration Loader,"Create a class that loads configuration first from system properties, and if not found, falls back to environment variables."
The System Class Methods,Final Project - File Concatenator,"Write a program that takes two filenames as arguments, redirects `System.in` to each file in turn, and writes the combined output to `System.out`."
The System Class Methods,Final Project - Simple Process Timer,"Create a command-line utility that runs another command and uses `System.nanoTime()` to report how long the command took to execute."
The System Class Methods,Non-zero exit code,"Write a script or program that checks the exit code of your Java application after it terminates with `System.exit(123)`."
The System Class Methods,Parsing the Java version string,"Get the `java.version` property and write code to parse out just the major version number."
The System Class Methods,Passing Properties via Command Line,"Run a Java program from the command line with the `-D` flag (e.g., `-Dmykey=myvalue`) and retrieve it using `System.getProperty()`."
The System Class Methods,Printing `System.getProperties()` to a file,"Redirect `System.out`, then call `System.getProperties().list(System.out)` to save all properties to a file."
The System Class Methods,Private constructor,"Explain in comments why the `System` class has a private constructor."
The System Class Methods,Reading from redirected `System.in`,"Write a program that reads all lines from `System.in` and prints them. Test it by piping a file to it from the command line."
The System Class Methods,Restoring standard streams,"After redirecting `System.out`, store the original `PrintStream` in a variable so you can set it back later."
The System Class Methods,Security - getSecurityManager(),"Call `System.getSecurityManager()` to get the system security manager. Note that this is deprecated for removal."
The System Class Methods,Standard streams are static,"Explain why `System.out`, `System.in`, and `System.err` are `static` fields."
The System Class Methods,Timing a `Thread.sleep()` call,"Use `System.nanoTime()` to measure the actual time a thread sleeps versus the requested time."
The System Class Methods,Using `Properties` object,"Get the system `Properties` object, add a new property, and then use `System.getProperty()` to retrieve it."
