This Keyword,Anonymous Inner Class,"Use 'this' inside an anonymous inner class to refer to the inner class instance, and 'ClassName.this' to refer to the outer class instance."
This Keyword,Avoiding Name Conflicts,"Create a method that has a local variable with the same name as an instance variable. Use 'this' to explicitly refer to the instance variable."
This Keyword,Call Another Constructor,"Create a class with two constructors. Have one constructor call the other using 'this()' to reduce code duplication."
This Keyword,Distinguish Instance Variables,"In a constructor for a 'Person' class, use 'this' to assign parameter values (e.g. 'name', 'age') to instance variables with the same names (this.name = name)."
This Keyword,Explicitly Calling a Method,"Although not necessary, show how 'this.myMethod()' is equivalent to just 'myMethod()' when calling another method of the same object."
This Keyword,In a Constructor for a Helper Method,"Call a private helper method from within a constructor, passing 'this' to the helper method so it can operate on the newly created object."
This Keyword,In a Setter Method,"In a setter method, like 'setName(String name)', use 'this.name = name' to assign the new value to the instance variable."
This Keyword,In equals() Method,"When overriding the 'equals(Object obj)' method, use 'this == obj' as the first check for reference equality."
This Keyword,In toString() Method,"When overriding the 'toString()' method, use 'this' implicitly or explicitly to access the instance variables to build the string representation."
This Keyword,Pass as an Argument,"Create a method that takes an object of the current class as an argument. From another method in the same class, call the first method, passing 'this' as the argument."
This Keyword,Return the Current Instance,"Create a method with a fluent interface style that returns 'this' (the current object) to allow for method chaining (e.g. object.setX(10).setY(20);)."
This Keyword,Static Context Error,"Try to use the 'this' keyword inside a static method and observe the compiler error. Explain why 'this' cannot be used in a static context."
Threads,"'Thread.UncaughtExceptionHandler'","Create a thread that throws an unchecked 'RuntimeException' from its 'run()' method. Attach a 'Thread.UncaughtExceptionHandler' to this thread to catch the exception and log a custom error message."
Threads,"'ThreadLocal' for Thread-Specific Data","Create a 'ThreadLocal<Integer>' variable. Start multiple threads that each set a unique value (e.g., their thread ID) to this variable. Show that each thread can only access its own value and does not see the values set by other threads."
Threads,"'join()' with a Timeout","Start a worker thread that sleeps for 5 seconds. The main thread should call 'worker.join(2000)' (a 2-second timeout). The main thread should then print whether the worker is still alive ('isAlive()') to show that the join timed out."
Threads,"'notify()' vs. 'notifyAll()'","Create a scenario with one producer and three consumer threads waiting on the same lock. First, use 'notify()' in the producer. Observe that only one consumer wakes up. Then, change it to 'notifyAll()' and observe that all consumers wake up (though only one will get the lock)."
Threads,"'start()' vs. 'run()' Method","Create a simple 'Runnable'. In your main method, create two threads with this 'Runnable'. Call 'start()' on the first thread and 'run()' directly on the second. Observe and explain the difference in output and execution flow."
Threads,"Bank Account Simulation","Create a 'BankAccount' class with synchronized 'deposit()' and 'withdraw()' methods. Create multiple 'Customer' threads that randomly deposit and withdraw money from the same account, demonstrating thread-safe state modification."
Threads,"Callable and Future for Result Retrieval","Rewrite the 'Retrieving Data from a Thread' exercise using 'ExecutorService' and 'Callable<V>'. Submit the 'Callable' to get a 'Future<V>' object. Use 'future.get()' to retrieve the result, which blocks until the computation is complete."
Threads,"Completing a Future Manually","Create a 'CompletableFuture' and pass it to a worker thread. The worker thread performs a calculation and then completes the future using 'future.complete(result)'. The main thread can then get the result without needing to 'join()' the worker thread directly."
Threads,"Condition Variables","Rewrite the Producer-Consumer problem using 'ReentrantLock' and its associated 'Condition' objects ('await()', 'signal()', 'signalAll()'). This demonstrates a more flexible alternative to intrinsic 'wait()' and 'notify()'."
Threads,"Cooperative Thread Cancellation","Implement a thread that runs a long loop (e.g., 'while (!Thread.currentThread().isInterrupted())'). The main thread should let it run for a while and then call 'interrupt()'. The loop should terminate gracefully because its condition checks the interrupted status."
Threads,"Create Thread by Extending 'Thread' Class","Create a class 'MyThread' that extends 'java.lang.Thread'. Override the 'run()' method to print numbers from 1 to 10. In your main method, create an instance of 'MyThread' and start it."
Threads,"Create Thread by Implementing 'Runnable'","Create a class 'MyRunnable' that implements the 'java.lang.Runnable' interface. Implement the 'run()' method to print the alphabet from A to Z. In 'main', create a 'Thread' instance, pass 'MyRunnable' to its constructor, and start the thread."
Threads,"Creating a Deadlock","Write a program where two threads each attempt to acquire two locks in opposite order. Thread A locks Lock1 then Lock2. Thread B locks Lock2 then Lock1. Run the program to demonstrate a deadlock, then use 'jstack' to analyze it."
Threads,"Daemon vs. User Threads","Create a 'worker' thread that runs an infinite loop. In 'main', start this thread. Observe that the program never exits. Now, call 'worker.setDaemon(true)' before starting it. Observe that the JVM now exits even though the worker is still 'running'."
Threads,"ForkJoinPool for Recursive Tasks","Implement a recursive task, like calculating Fibonacci numbers or sorting a large array (Merge Sort). Use the 'ForkJoinPool' and 'RecursiveTask' to parallelize the computation by breaking the problem into smaller subtasks."
Threads,"Grouping Threads with 'ThreadGroup'","Create a 'ThreadGroup'. Instantiate several threads, passing the group to their constructors. Write code that uses the 'ThreadGroup' to interrupt all threads in the group with a single method call."
Threads,"InheritableThreadLocal","Create an 'InheritableThreadLocal' variable in the main thread and set a value. Start a new child thread from the main thread. Show that the child thread automatically inherits the value from its parent."
Threads,"Interrupting a Sleeping Thread","Create a thread that sleeps for 10 seconds. The main thread should start it, wait for 2 seconds, and then call 'interrupt()' on the sleeping thread. The sleeping thread's 'catch' block for 'InterruptedException' should print a message indicating it was interrupted."
Threads,"Listing All Active Threads","Write a program that uses 'Thread.getAllStackTraces().keySet()' to get a set of all currently active threads in the JVM. Iterate through the set and print the name, state, and priority of each thread."
Threads,"Multithreaded Prime Number Finder","Write a program that finds all prime numbers up to a given number N. Divide the range of numbers among several worker threads to speed up the calculation. The main thread should collect and combine the results."
Threads,"Passing Data to a Thread via Constructor","Create a 'Runnable' class that accepts data (e.g., a string message) through its constructor and stores it in a private field. The 'run()' method should then use this data."
Threads,"Pausing Execution with 'Thread.sleep()'","Write a program where the main thread starts a new thread. The new thread should loop 10 times, printing a message and then sleeping for 500 milliseconds in each iteration using 'Thread.sleep()'."
Threads,"Producer-Consumer with 'wait()' and 'notify()'","Implement the classic Producer-Consumer problem. Use a shared list (the buffer), a 'Producer' thread that adds items, and a 'Consumer' thread that removes them. Use 'synchronized', 'wait()', and 'notify()' for coordination."
Threads,"Race Condition Demonstration","Create a 'Counter' class with a non-synchronized 'increment()' method. Start 10 threads that each call this method 1,000 times on the same 'Counter' instance. Print the final count and observe that it is not the expected 10,000 due to a race condition."
Threads,"ReadWriteLock for Concurrent Reading","Implement a data structure that is read frequently but written to infrequently. Use a 'java.util.concurrent.locks.ReadWriteLock' to allow multiple reader threads to access the data concurrently, while writer threads still have exclusive access."
Threads,"ReentrantLock as an Alternative to 'synchronized'","Rewrite the 'Counter' exercise using 'java.util.concurrent.locks.ReentrantLock'. Show how to use 'lock()' and 'unlock()' in a 'try-finally' block to achieve the same thread safety as a 'synchronized' method."
Threads,"Retrieving Data from a Thread","Design a worker thread that computes a result. The 'Runnable' should store the result in a field. The main thread should start the worker, 'join()' it, and then call a getter method on the 'Runnable' instance to retrieve the result after the thread has finished."
Threads,"Setting Thread Names","Create and start five threads. In the constructor of your 'Runnable', use 'Thread.currentThread().setName()' to give each thread a unique name (e.g., 'Worker-1', 'Worker-2'). The 'run()' method should print the thread's name."
Threads,"Simple Animation with a Thread","Using a simple graphics library like Swing, create a component that has a ball. Use a separate thread to continuously update the ball's position and call 'repaint()', creating a simple animation. (Add comments about Swing's single-thread rule)."
Threads,"Simple Blocking Queue with 'wait()' and 'notifyAll()'","Implement a thread-safe blocking queue of a fixed size from scratch. The 'put()' method should block if the queue is full, and the 'take()' method should block if it's empty. Use 'wait()', 'notifyAll()', and a shared lock."
Threads,"Simulating a Barrier","Implement a barrier where a number of threads must all reach a certain point of execution before any of them are allowed to proceed. Simulate this using a shared counter and 'wait()'/'notifyAll()'."
Threads,"Simulating a Livelock","Create a scenario with two threads that are overly polite. Thread A needs a resource held by B, and B needs a resource held by A. Both threads try to acquire the other's lock, but if they fail, they release their own lock and try again. They are active but make no progress."
Threads,"Spurious Wakeups and the 'wait()' Loop","In the Consumer part of the Producer-Consumer problem, ensure the 'wait()' call is inside a 'while' loop ('while (buffer.isEmpty()) { wait(); }'). Add comments to explain why this is necessary to guard against spurious wakeups."
Threads,"Stopping a Thread (Deprecated 'stop()' vs. Cooperative)","Discuss why 'Thread.stop()' is deprecated. Then, implement two versions of a stoppable thread: one that uses the unsafe 'stop()' method (for demonstration only), and a correct one that uses a 'volatile boolean' flag for cooperative cancellation."
Threads,"Synchronization on a Private Lock Object","Improve the previous exercise by creating a 'private final Object lock = new Object();'. Use 'synchronized(lock)' instead of 'synchronized(this)'. Explain the benefits of using a private lock object."
Threads,"Synchronized Block","Create a class with two different methods that modify shared data. Instead of synchronizing the entire methods, use a 'synchronized(this)' block to protect only the critical sections of code within each method."
Threads,"Synchronized Method to Prevent Race Condition","Fix the previous exercise by declaring the 'increment()' method with the 'synchronized' keyword. Run the program again and verify that the final count is now consistently 10,000."
Threads,"Synchronizing Static Methods","Create a class with a 'static' counter variable and a 'static synchronized' method to increment it. Start multiple threads that call this static method and verify that the final count is correct, demonstrating synchronization on the class-level lock."
Threads,"The 'yield()' Method","Create two threads that print messages. In the run loop of one thread, call 'Thread.yield()'. Discuss that 'yield()' is a hint to the scheduler to run another thread, but its behavior is not guaranteed."
Threads,"Thread CPU Time Measurement","Use 'java.lang.management.ThreadMXBean' to get the total CPU time consumed by a specific thread. This can be used to profile the performance of different parts of a multithreaded application."
Threads,"Thread Dump Analysis","Run the deadlock program you created earlier. While it is stuck, use the 'jstack <pid>' command-line tool to generate a thread dump. Analyze the output to find the deadlock information."
Threads,"Thread Interrupts vs. a 'volatile' Flag","Create two versions of a cancellable task. One uses 'Thread.interrupt()' to signal cancellation. The other uses a 'volatile boolean' flag. Discuss the pros and cons of each approach, especially how interrupts handle blocking calls."
Threads,"Thread Lifecycle Hooks","Create a custom 'Thread' subclass that overrides the 'run()' method. In your 'run()' method, use a 'try-finally' block to implement 'beforeExecute()' and 'afterExecute()' logic, which runs before and after the main task."
Threads,"Thread Priority","Create two threads of the same 'Runnable' type. Use 'setPriority()' to give one thread 'Thread.MIN_PRIORITY' and the other 'Thread.MAX_PRIORITY'. Have both threads perform a CPU-intensive task. Observe the output to see if priority affects scheduling (results may vary by OS)."
Threads,"Thread States","Write a program that creates a new thread. Print its state ('getState()') at various points: after creation (NEW), after 'start()' (RUNNABLE), while it is sleeping (TIMED_WAITING), and after it has finished (TERMINATED)."
Threads,"Thread contention monitoring","Use 'ThreadMXBean' to monitor thread contention by checking 'getThreadInfo(...).getLockOwnerName()' and 'getLockName()'. Write a program that creates lock contention and a separate monitoring thread to report on it."
Threads,"Virtual Threads (Project Loom) Introduction","Using a JDK with Project Loom, rewrite an application that creates thousands of platform threads for blocking tasks. Change it to use virtual threads ('Thread.startVirtualThread()') and observe the significant reduction in memory usage and improved performance."
Threads,"Volatile Keyword Demonstration","Create a shared 'boolean flag' variable. One thread sets the flag to 'true' after a delay. Another thread loops until it sees the flag as 'true'. First, run without 'volatile' and observe it may loop forever. Then, add 'volatile' and show that the change is correctly visible."
Threads,"Waiting for a Thread to Finish with 'join()'","Create a worker thread that simulates a long task (e.g., by sleeping for 3 seconds). The main thread should start the worker thread, print a message 'Starting worker...', call 'join()' on the worker thread, and then print 'Worker finished.' only after the worker has completed."
Threads,"Web Crawler with Threads","Build a simple web crawler. Start with a single URL. One or more threads should download the page, parse it for new URLs, and add those to a shared, thread-safe queue of URLs to be visited. The process repeats until the queue is empty or a depth limit is reached."
Type Casting,"ExplicitCasting","Assign a 'double' value to an 'int' variable using an explicit cast. Print the result to show truncation."
Type Casting,"ImplicitCasting","Assign an 'int' value to a 'double' variable and print the result to demonstrate widening conversion."
Type Casting,Casting Characters to Integers,"Declare a 'char' variable. Cast it to an 'int' to get its ASCII/Unicode value."
Type Casting,Casting Integers to Characters,"Declare an 'int' variable with a value corresponding to an ASCII character (e.g. 65 for 'A'). Cast it to a 'char' and print the result."
Type Casting,Casting Primitives to Wrappers,"Demonstrate how casting works with wrapper classes, for example, casting an 'Integer' to a 'Double' is not possible directly, but you can get the 'intValue()' and then cast the primitive."
Type Casting,Casting in Expressions,"Write an expression to calculate the average of three integers. Cast one of the integers to a 'double' before the division to get a floating-point result instead of an integer result."
Type Casting,Casting in Method Calls,"Create an overloaded method, one that takes an 'int' and one that takes a 'double'. Call the method with an 'int' variable, and then call it by casting the 'int' variable to a 'double'."
Type Casting,Casting with Objects (Downcasting),"Using the 'Animal' reference from the previous exercise that holds a 'Dog' object, explicitly cast it back to a 'Dog' reference variable (downcasting). Use 'instanceof' to check before casting."
Type Casting,Casting with Objects (Upcasting),"Create a 'Dog' class that inherits from an 'Animal' class. Create a 'Dog' object and assign it to an 'Animal' reference variable (upcasting)."
Type Casting,ClassCastException,"Create an 'Animal' reference holding a 'Cat' object. Try to downcast it to a 'Dog' reference to see the 'ClassCastException' at runtime."
Type Casting,Explicit Casting (Narrowing),"Declare a 'double' and an 'int'. Explicitly cast the 'double' to an 'int' and print the result to see the truncation of the decimal part."
Type Casting,Implicit Casting (Widening),"Declare a 'byte', 'short', and 'int'. Assign the 'byte' to the 'short', and the 'short' to the 'int'. Print the values to show implicit casting."
Type Casting,Potential Data Loss,"Explicitly cast a 'long' value that is larger than the maximum 'int' value to an 'int'. Print the result to demonstrate data loss."
Type Casting,Rounding with Casting,"Show how to round a 'double' to the nearest 'int' by adding 0.5 and then casting to 'int'."
Type Inference,"SimpleVar","Use the 'var' keyword to declare and initialize a String. Print its class using '.getClass().getName()'."
Type Inference,"VarAndNull","Try to initialize a 'var' variable with 'null'. Explain the resulting error."
Type Inference,"VarLimitations","Try to declare a variable using 'var' without initializing it. Observe and explain the compiler error."
Type Inference,"VarWithPrimitives","Use 'var' to declare a variable initialized with an integer literal. What is its inferred type?"
Types,Boolean Flags,"Create a program that uses boolean variables as flags to control the flow of execution in an if-else statement."
Types,Byte for File I/O,"Simulate reading a byte from a file by declaring a byte variable and assigning it a value between -128 and 127."
Types,Character to Integer,"Declare a character variable and assign it a letter. Then, assign the character variable to an integer variable and print the integer value to see its ASCII representation."
Types,Data Type Mismatch Error,"Write a program that intentionally tries to assign a value of a larger data type to a smaller data type without casting and observe the compiler error. Comment on the reason for the error."
Types,Data Type Ranges,"Write a program that prints the minimum and maximum values for each primitive data type (byte, short, int, long, float, double)."
Types,Default Values,"Declare instance variables of each primitive data type in a class but do not initialize them. Create an object of the class and print the default values of these variables."
Types,Floating-Point Precision,"Declare float and double variables with the same fractional value. Perform a calculation and observe the difference in precision."
Types,Long for Large Numbers,"Use a long data type to store and calculate the factorial of a number like 20, which would overflow an int."
Types,Primitive vs. Wrapper,"Declare a primitive int and an Integer wrapper class object. Demonstrate autoboxing and unboxing by assigning between them."
Types,Scientific Notation,"Declare a double variable and initialize it using scientific notation (e.g. 1.23e4). Print the value to the console."
Types,Short for Memory Saving,"Imagine a scenario where memory is limited. Declare an array of 'short' to store a large number of values that fit within its range, and comment on the memory savings compared to 'int'."
Types,Type Conversion,"Declare a variable of each primitive data type and try to assign it to every other primitive data type to observe which conversions are implicit and which require explicit casting."
Underscore Literals,"NumericLiterals","Declare a 'long' variable for one million using underscores for readability (e.g. '1_000_000')."
Uninitialized Local,"UninitializedLocalError","Declare a local variable inside a method but do not initialize it. Try to use it in a 'println' statement and observe the compile-time error."
Var With Object,"VarAndObjectCreation","Use 'var' to declare a variable that holds a new instance of a custom class you create."
Variables,Final Variable,"Declare a final variable and initialize it. Try to reassign it a new value and observe the compiler error. Explain the concept of a constant."
Variables,Instance vs. Static Variables,"Create a class with both an instance variable and a static variable. Create multiple objects of the class, change the instance variable for one object, and change the static variable. Print the variables for all objects to see the difference."
Variables,Naming Convention Practice,"Declare variables for a user's first name, last name, age, and isStudent status, following Java's naming conventions for variables."
Variables,Static Variable Counter,"Create a class with a static variable that acts as a counter. Increment this counter every time a new object of the class is created. Print the counter's value to see how many objects have been created."
Variables,Type Inference with 'var',"If using Java 10 or later, declare a few local variables using the 'var' keyword and let the compiler infer the type. Print the class of each variable to confirm its type."
Variables,Uninitialized Variable Error,"Declare a local variable but do not initialize it. Try to use it in an expression and observe the compiler error. Comment on why this happens."
Variables,Variable Assignment,"Declare variables and then assign values to them in separate statements. Print their values."
Variables,Variable Initialization,"Declare variables of different data types and initialize them at the time of declaration. Print their values."
Variables,Variable Lifetime,"Write a method that declares a local variable. Call this method multiple times and observe that the local variable is created and destroyed with each method call."
Variables,Variable Reassignment,"Declare a variable, assign it a value, print it, then reassign it a new value and print it again to show that variables can hold different values over time."
Variables,Variable Scope,"Create a class with a global variable, a local variable inside a method, and a block-level variable inside a loop. Print the values of these variables to understand their scope."
Variables,Variable Shadowing,"Create a class with an instance variable named 'x'. In a method within that class, declare a local variable also named 'x'. Demonstrate how the local variable 'shadows' the instance variable."
While Loop,"GuessTheNumber","Create a 'guess the number' game that uses a while loop to continue until the user guesses the correct number."
While Loop,"InputValidation","Use a while loop to repeatedly prompt a user for their age until they enter a value between 0 and 120."
While Loop,"PowerOfTwo","Use a while loop to find the first power of 2 that is greater than 1000."
While Loop,"ReverseAnInteger","Use a while loop to reverse the digits of an integer (e.g. 12345 becomes 54321)."
While Loop,"SentinelControlledSum","Write a program that uses a while loop to read numbers from the user until they enter -1, then prints the sum of all numbers entered."
While Loop,"SimpleMenuLoop","Create a text-based menu that loops with a while loop, asking for user input until they select the 'exit' option."
Widening And Narrowing,"DataLossExample","Cast a 'long' value that is larger than 'Integer.MAX_VALUE' to an 'int' and print the result to demonstrate data loss."
Wrapper Classes,ArrayList of Integers,"Create an ArrayList that can hold integers. Add some integers to it (demonstrating autoboxing) and then retrieve and print them (demonstrating unboxing)."
Wrapper Classes,Autoboxing and Unboxing,"Declare a primitive int and an Integer object. Demonstrate autoboxing by assigning the primitive to the object and unboxing by assigning the object to the primitive."
Wrapper Classes,Boolean Wrapper,"Use the Boolean wrapper class to parse a string ('true' or 'false') into a boolean value."
Wrapper Classes,Character Wrapper Methods,"Use the Character wrapper class to check if a character is a digit (isDigit), a letter (isLetter), or whitespace (isWhitespace)."
Wrapper Classes,Comparing Wrapper Objects,"Create two Integer objects with the same value. Compare them using '==' and the '.equals()' method. Explain the difference in the output."
Wrapper Classes,Custom Wrapper Method,"Create a utility class with a static method that takes an int array and returns an Integer array. This will require manual boxing in a loop."
Wrapper Classes,Null Wrapper Reference,"Declare a wrapper class variable (e.g. Double) and assign it the value null. Try to unbox it to a primitive double and observe the NullPointerException."
Wrapper Classes,Number Superclass,"Create a method that accepts a Number object (the superclass of all numeric wrapper classes). Pass in an Integer, a Double, and a Float to demonstrate polymorphism."
Wrapper Classes,Parsing with a Radix,"Use the Integer.parseInt(String s, int radix) method to parse a binary string and a hexadecimal string into an integer."
Wrapper Classes,Wrapper Class Methods,"Use the Integer wrapper class to convert a string to an int (parseInt), an int to a string (toString), and to find the min/max of two numbers (min, max)."
Wrapper Classes,Wrapper Constants,"Print the values of constants like Integer.MAX_VALUE, Integer.MIN_VALUE, Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY, and Double.NaN."
Writing Classes,Class Blueprint,"Write a 'House' class with attributes for number of bedrooms, number of bathrooms, and square footage. Include a default constructor and a parameterized constructor."
Writing Classes,Class with a 'finalize' method,"Create a class and override the 'finalize()' method to print a message when the object is about to be garbage collected (Note: Explain that this is not a reliable mechanism for resource cleanup)."
Writing Classes,Class with an Enum,"Create an 'enum' for 'DayOfWeek'. Then, create a 'Meeting' class that has a 'DayOfWeek' attribute to specify on which day the meeting occurs."
Writing Classes,Constructor Overloading,"Create a 'Pizza' class with multiple constructors: a default constructor for a plaiGn cheese pizza, one that takes toppings, and one that takes toppings and size."
Writing Classes,Copy Constructor,"In a 'Point' class, create a copy constructor that takes another 'Point' object and initializes the new object's attributes with the values from the existing object."
Writing Classes,Data Hiding,"Create a 'Person' class with private attributes for name and social security number. Provide a public method to get the name but no public method to get the social security number, demonstrating data hiding."
Writing Classes,Fluent Interface,"Design a 'PersonBuilder' class with a fluent interface. For example, 'new PersonBuilder().withName("
Writing Classes,Immutable Class,"Write an immutable 'Color' class with final attributes for red, green, and blue values. The values should be set only through the constructor."
Writing Classes,Inner Class,"Create an 'Outer' class with a private method. Then, create an 'Inner' class inside the 'Outer' class that can access the private method of the 'Outer' class."
Writing Classes,Overriding equals() and hashCode() ,"In a 'Student' class, override the 'equals()' and 'hashCode()' methods to base equality on the student's ID number, not on the object reference."
Writing Classes,Singleton Pattern,"Implement the Singleton pattern for a 'DatabaseConnection' class to ensure that only one instance of the class can ever be created."
Writing Classes,Static Utility Class,"Create a 'MathUtils' class that is not meant to be instantiated (give it a private constructor). Add static methods for operations like finding the factorial of a number or checking if a number is prime."
