Basic Class Design,"Simple Chalk","Create a `Chalk` class with `color` and `length`. Include a `drawOnSidewalk()` method that reduces its length. The test should draw with the chalk."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Crayon","Design a `Crayon` class with `color` and `sharpness`. Include a `sharpen()` method. The test should sharpen the crayon."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Glitter","Create a `Glitter` class with `color` and `particleSize`. Include a `sprinkle()` method. The test should sprinkle glitter on a project."
Basic Class Design,"Artist's Easel","Design an `Easel` class with `height` and a `canvasAttached`. Include an `attachCanvas()` method. The test should attach a canvas to the easel."
Basic Class Design,"Mythical Griffin","Create a `Griffin` class with `name` and `wingSpan`. Include a `fly()` method. The test should make the griffin fly."
Basic Class Design,"Mythical Fairy","Design a `Fairy` class with `wingColor` and `magicType`. Include a `castSpell()` method. The test should cast a fairy spell."
Basic Class Design,"Mythical Genie","Create a `Genie` class with `lampColor` and `wishesRemaining`. Include a `grantWish()` method that decrements the wish count. The test should grant a wish."
Basic Class Design,"Mythical Leprechaun","Design a `Leprechaun` class with `goldPotAmount` and `hatColor`. Include a `hideGold()` method. The test should hide the pot of gold."
Basic Class Design,"Mythical Troll","Create a `Troll` class with `name` and `bridgeLocation`. Include a `guardBridge()` method. The test should have the troll guard its bridge."
Basic Class Design,"Ancient Scroll","Design a `Scroll` class with `text` and `material` (e.g., 'Papyrus'). Include `roll()` and `unroll()` methods. The test should unroll the scroll to read it."
Basic Class Design,"Roman Chariot","Create a `Chariot` class with `horseCount` and `wheelDiameter`. Include a `race()` method. The test should race the chariot."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Catapult","Design a `Catapult` class with `projectileType` and `range`. Include a `launch()` method. The test should launch a projectile."
Basic Class Design,"Ancient Astrolabe","Create an `Astrolabe` class with `material` and `currentStar`. Include a `calculatePosition()` method. The test should use it to navigate."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Windmill","Design a `Windmill` class with `bladeCount` and `rotationSpeed`. Include a `spin()` method. The test should make the windmill spin."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Lighthouse","Create a `Lighthouse` class with `height` and a boolean `isLightOn`. Include `turnLightOn()` and `turnLightOff()` methods. The test should turn on the light."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Well","Design a `Well` class with `depth` and `waterLevel`. Include a `fetchWater()` method. The test should fetch a bucket of water from the well."
Basic Class Design,"Castle Tower","Create a `Tower` class with `height` and `stoneType`. Include a `defend()` method. The test should create a castle tower."
Basic Class Design,"Castle Moat","Design a `Moat` class with `width` and `waterDepth`. Include a `fillWithWater()` method. The test should fill the moat."
Basic Class Design,"Viking Longship","Create a `Longship` class with `oarCount` and `sailColor`. Include a `row()` method. The test should row the longship."
Basic Class Design,"Knight's Shield","Design a `Shield` class with `material` and `crestDesign`. Include a `blockAttack()` method. The test should block with the shield."
Basic Class Design,"Samurai Sword","Create a `Katana` class with `bladeLength` and `handleWrapColor`. Include a `drawSword()` method. The test should draw the katana."
Basic Class Design,"Egyptian Pyramid","Design a `Pyramid` class with `height` and `pharaohName`. Include a `storeTreasure()` method. The test should create the Great Pyramid."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Igloo","Create an `Igloo` class with `diameter` and `blockCount`. Include a `provideShelter()` method. The test should create an igloo."
Basic Class Design,"Totem Pole","Design a `TotemPole` class with `height` and `animalCarvings`. Include a `tellStory()` method. The test should create a totem pole."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Teepee","Create a `Teepee` class with `poleCount` and `coverMaterial`. Include a `setup()` method. The test should set up the teepee."
Basic Class Design,"Boomerang","Design a `Boomerang` class with `woodType` and `arcShape`. Include a `throw()` method that prints 'The boomerang returns!'. The test should throw the boomerang."
Basic Class Design,"Peace Pipe","Create a `PeacePipe` class with `material` and `decoration`. Include a `smoke()` method. The test should create a peace pipe."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Abacus","Design an `Abacus` class with `rodCount` and `beadColor`. Include a `calculate()` method. The test should use the abacus to add two numbers."
Basic Class Design,"Conestoga Wagon","Create a `Wagon` class with `wheelCount` and `canvasCover`. Include a `travel()` method. The test should simulate traveling the Oregon Trail."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Telegraph","Design a `Telegraph` class with `key` and `sounder`. Include a `sendMorseCode(message)` method. The test should send a message."
Basic Class Design,"Old-Timey Radio","Create a `Radio` class with `frequency` and `volumeKnob`. Include a `tuneIn(station)` method. The test should tune in to a radio station."
Basic Class Design,"Rotary Phone","Design a `RotaryPhone` class with `color` and `numberDialed`. Include a `dialNumber()` method. The test should dial a number."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Typewriter","Create a `Typewriter` class with `keyCount` and `inkRibbonColor`. Include a `typeLetter(character)` method. The test should type a sentence."
Basic Class Design,"Film Projector","Design a `FilmProjector` class with `reelSize` and a boolean `isPlaying`. Include `play()` and `stop()` methods. The test should play a film."
Basic Class Design,"Vinyl Record","Create a `VinylRecord` class with `artist` and `albumTitle`. Include a `playOnTurntable()` method. The test should play the record."
Basic Class Design,"Pocket Watch","Design a `PocketWatch` class with `material` and `time`. Include a `checkTime()` method. The test should check the time on the pocket watch."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Fountain","Create a `Fountain` class with `waterSource` and `sculpture`. Include a `sprayWater()` method. The test should turn on the fountain."
Basic Class Design,"Park Bench","Design a `ParkBench` class with `material` and `seatingCapacity`. Include a `sit()` method. The test should create a park bench."
Basic Class Design,"Swing Set","Create a `SwingSet` class with `swingCount` and `height`. Include a `swing()` method. The test should simulate someone swinging."
Basic Class Design,"Carousel","Design a `Carousel` class with `horseCount` and `music`. Include a `rotate()` method. The test should start the carousel."
Basic Class Design,"Ferris Wheel","Create a `FerrisWheel` class with `carCount` and `height`. Include a `startRide()` method. The test should start the ferris wheel."
Basic Class Design,"Roller Coaster","Design a `RollerCoaster` class with `name` and `topSpeed`. Include a `ride()` method. The test should ride the roller coaster."
Basic Class Design,"Popcorn Machine","Create a `PopcornMachine` class with `kettleSize` and `butterDispenser`. Include a `makePopcorn()` method. The test should make a batch of popcorn."
Basic Class Design,"Cotton Candy Machine","Design a `CottonCandyMachine` class with `sugarColor` and a boolean `isSpinning`. Include a `makeFluff()` method. The test should make cotton candy."
Basic Class Design,"Ticket Booth","Create a `TicketBooth` class with `eventName` and `ticketPrice`. Include a `sellTicket()` method. The test should sell a ticket to the fair."
Basic Class Design,"Bumper Car","Design a `BumperCar` class with `color` and `speed`. Include a `bump(anotherCar)` method. The test should bump another car."
Basic Class Design,"Haunted House","Create a `HauntedHouse` class with `scareFactor` and `roomCount`. Include a `scareVisitor()` method. The test should scare a visitor."
Basic Class Design,"Funhouse Mirror","Design a `FunhouseMirror` class with `distortionType` ('Tall', 'Short', 'Wavy'). Include a `reflect()` method. The test should look into the mirror."
Basic Class Design,"Midway Game","Create a `MidwayGame` class with `name` (e.g., 'Ring Toss') and `prize`. Include a `playGame()` method. The test should play the game to win a prize."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Telescope","Design a `Telescope` class with `magnification` and `lensDiameter`. Include a `viewStars()` method. The test should use the telescope."
Basic Class Design,"Observatory","Create an `Observatory` class with `location` and `telescopeType`. Include an `openDome()` method. The test should open the observatory dome."
Basic Class Design,"Planetarium","Design a `Planetarium` class with `domeSize` and `showName`. Include a `startShow()` method. The test should start the planetarium show."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Antenna","Create an `Antenna` class with `height` and `frequencyRange`. Include a `receiveSignal()` method. The test should receive a signal."
Basic Class Design,"Lab Beaker","Design a `Beaker` class with `capacityInML` and `contents`. Include a `pourInto(anotherBeaker)` method. The test should pour liquid from one beaker to another."
Basic Class Design,"Bunsen Burner","Create a `BunsenBurner` class with `gasType` and a boolean `isLit`. Include `light()` and `extinguish()` methods. The test should light the burner."
Basic Class Design,"Test Tube","Design a `TestTube` class with `volume` and `liquidColor`. Include a `heat()` method. The test should heat the contents of the test tube."
Basic Class Design,"Petri Dish","Create a `PetriDish` class with `cultureMedium` and `bacteriaGrowth`. Include a `growCulture()` method. The test should grow a culture."
Basic Class Design,"Graduated Cylinder","Design a `GraduatedCylinder` class with `maxVolume` and `currentVolume`. Include a `measureLiquid()` method. The test should measure a specific volume."
Basic Class Design,"Lab Coat","Create a `LabCoat` class with `size` and `numberOfPockets`. Include a `wear()` method. The test should put on the lab coat."
Basic Class Design,"Safety Goggles","Design a `SafetyGoggles` class with `lensMaterial` and `strapColor`. Include a `putOn()` method. The test should put on the goggles for an experiment."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Algorithm","Create an `Algorithm` class with `name` and `complexity`. Include an `execute()` method. The test should execute a 'Bubble Sort' algorithm."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Variable","Design a `Variable` class with `name`, `dataType`, and `value`. Include a `setValue(newValue)` method. The test should create and update a variable."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Function","Create a `Function` class with `name` and `parameterCount`. Include a `call()` method. The test should call a function."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Loop","Design a `Loop` class with `loopType` ('For', 'While') and `iterationCount`. Include a `runLoop()` method. The test should run a 'For' loop 10 times."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Conditional","Create a `Conditional` class with `condition` (a string) and `isTrue`. Include an `evaluate()` method. The test should evaluate an 'if' statement."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Database","Design a `Database` class with `name` and `tableCount`. Include a `connect()` method. The test should connect to the database."
Basic Class Design,"Database Table","Create a `Table` class with `name` and `rowCount`. Include a `query()` method. The test should run a query on the table."
Basic Class Design,"API Endpoint","Design an `APIEndpoint` class with `url` and `requestType` ('GET', 'POST'). Include a `makeRequest()` method. The test should make a 'GET' request."
Basic Class Design,"JSON Object","Create a `JSONObject` class with `keyCount` and `data`. Include a `parse()` method. The test should parse a simple JSON string."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Cookie","Design a `Cookie` class (web context) with `name` and `value`. Include a `setInBrowser()` method. The test should set a cookie."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Server","Create a `Server` class with `ipAddress` and `status` ('Online', 'Offline'). Include a `ping()` method. The test should ping the server."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Router","Design a `Router` class with `ssid` and `password`. Include a `broadcastSignal()` method. The test should broadcast a WiFi signal."
Basic Class Design,"Firewall Rule","Create a `FirewallRule` class with `portNumber` and `protocol` ('TCP', 'UDP'). Include an `applyRule()` method. The test should apply a firewall rule."
Basic Class Design,"Validated User Profile","Create a `UserProfile` class with private attributes for `username`, `email`, and `birthDate`. Provide public getters and setters. The `username` setter must ensure the name is between 4 and 15 characters. The `email` setter must ensure it contains an '@' symbol. The `birthDate` setter must ensure the date is in the past (before today, September 27, 2025). The test should attempt to set both valid and invalid data for each attribute."
Basic Class Design,"Immutable RGB Color","Design an immutable `RGBColor` class with private final attributes for `red`, `green`, and `blue`. The constructor should accept these three values and validate that each is within the 0-255 range, throwing an exception for invalid values. Include a `getHexString()` method that returns the color as a hex string (e.g., '#FF0000'). The test should create valid colors and attempt to create an invalid one in a try-catch block."
Basic Class Design,"Shopping Cart with Items","Design two classes: `CartItem` and `ShoppingCart`. `CartItem` has `itemName`, `unitPrice`, and `quantity`. `ShoppingCart` manages a list of `CartItem` objects. `ShoppingCart` should have methods `addItem(item)`, `removeItem(itemName)`, and `calculateTotal()`. The test should create a cart, add multiple items, remove one, and calculate the final total price."
Basic Class Design,"Vending Machine","Design a `VendingMachine` class that manages a collection of `Product` objects (with `name`, `price`, `quantity`). The machine should have methods `insertMoney(amount)`, `selectProduct(name)`, and `getChange()`. The machine must track inserted money and product inventory, handling cases where a product is out of stock or insufficient money is inserted. The test should simulate a full purchase cycle."
Basic Class Design,"Unique ID Generator","Create a `Widget` class with a private static integer `idCounter` initialized to 1000. Each time a new `Widget` is created (in its constructor), it should be assigned a unique ID from the counter, and the counter should be incremented. The class should also have a public getter for the ID. The test should create several `Widget` objects and print their unique IDs to verify they are sequential (1000, 1001, 1002, etc.)."
Basic Class Design,"Financial Account Hierarchy","Create a base class `Account` with `accountNumber` and `balance`. Add `deposit` and `withdraw` methods. Create two derived classes: `SavingsAccount` and `CheckingAccount`. `SavingsAccount` should have an `interestRate` attribute and a method to `applyInterest`. `CheckingAccount` should have an `overdraftLimit` attribute and override the `withdraw` method to allow for overdrafts up to that limit. The test should demonstrate the unique features of both account types."
Basic Class Design,"University Enrollment System","Design `Student`, `Course`, and `Enrollment` classes. A `Student` has a `studentId` and `name`. A `Course` has a `courseCode` and `courseName`. The `Enrollment` class manages a list of students enrolled in a list of courses. Use composition. The `Student` class should use a static counter for `studentId`. The `Course` class setter for `courseCode` must validate it follows a pattern (e.g., 'CS101'). The test should enroll several students in different courses and be able to list students by course."
Basic Class Design,"Flight Booking","Create a `Flight` class with private attributes for `flightNumber`, `departureCity`, `arrivalCity`, and `departureTime`. The `departureTime` must be in the future. The setters for `departureCity` and `arrivalCity` must ensure they are not the same. Provide a constructor to initialize these values and include validation. The test should create a valid flight and attempt to create flights with invalid data."
Basic Class Design,"Computer Configuration","Design `CPU`, `RAM`, and `Storage` classes with relevant attributes (e.g., `CPU` has `speedGHz`, `RAM` has `sizeGB`, `Storage` has `type` and `capacityGB`). Create a `Computer` class that is composed of one instance of each of these. The `Computer` class constructor should accept `CPU`, `RAM`, and `Storage` objects. Include a `displaySpecs()` method in the `Computer` class. The test should build and display the specs of two different computers."
Basic Class Design,"Math Constants Utility","Create a final class `MathConstants` that cannot be instantiated (private constructor). Inside, define public static final double variables for `PI`, `E`, and the `GOLDEN_RATIO`. The test should access these constants directly through the class name (e.g., `MathConstants.PI`) and use them in a calculation."
Basic Class Design,"Zoo Animal Hierarchy","Create an abstract base class `Animal` with an abstract method `speak()` and a concrete method `eat()`. Create three derived classes: `Lion`, `Penguin`, and `Parrot`. `Lion` should implement `speak()` to print 'Roar'. `Penguin` implements it to print 'Squawk'. `Parrot` implements it and also has a `learnPhrase(phrase)` method. The test should create a list of `Animal`s and loop through them, calling `speak()` to demonstrate polymorphism."
Basic Class Design,"Traffic Light Controller","Create a `TrafficLight` class with a state that can be `RED`, `YELLOW`, or `GREEN` (use an enum for the states). The class should have a `cycle()` method that advances the light to the next state in the correct order (GREEN -> YELLOW -> RED -> GREEN). Include a `getCurrentState()` method. The test should create a traffic light and call `cycle()` multiple times, printing the state after each call."
Basic Class Design,"Library Management","Design `Book`, `Author`, and `Library` classes. An `Author` has a `name` and `birthDate`. A `Book` is composed of an `Author` object and has a `title` and `isbn`. The `Library` manages a collection of `Book` objects. `Book`'s constructor must validate the `isbn` (e.g., must be 13 digits). The `Library` must have methods to `addBook`, `findBookByTitle`, and `listBooksByAuthor`. The test should populate and query the library."
Basic Class Design,"Pizza Builder","Design a `Pizza` class with attributes `size`, `crustType`, and a list of `toppings`. Create three constructors: one for a basic cheese pizza (requires only size and crust), one that accepts a list of toppings, and one that is a 'specialty' pizza that takes a name like 'Supreme' and pre-populates the toppings. The test should create one pizza using each constructor."
Basic Class Design,"Car and Engine","Create an `Engine` class with `horsepower` and `cylinders`. Create a `Car` class with `make`, `model`, and an `Engine` object. The `Car` class should have `start()` and `stop()` methods that internally call corresponding methods on its `Engine` object. The test should create a car with a specific engine and demonstrate starting and stopping it."
Basic Class Design,"Temperature Class","Create a `Temperature` class that stores temperature in Kelvin as a private attribute. Provide a constructor that takes a value and a unit ('C', 'F', or 'K'). Include public getter methods `getAsCelsius()`, `getAsFahrenheit()`, and `getAsKelvin()` that perform the necessary conversions. All calculations should be based on the internal Kelvin value. The test should create temperatures using different units and display them in all three units."
Basic Class Design,"Singleton Configuration","Implement a `ConfigurationManager` class using the Singleton pattern. It should hold application settings like `databaseURL` and `logLevel` in private attributes. It must have a private constructor and a public static `getInstance()` method. Add public getters and setters for the settings. The test should get the instance from two different places, change a setting through one reference, and verify the change is visible through the second reference."
Basic Class Design,"Employee Payroll System","Create a base `Employee` class with `name` and `id`. Create two derived classes: `SalariedEmployee` and `HourlyEmployee`. `SalariedEmployee` has a `monthlySalary`. `HourlyEmployee` has `hourlyRate` and `hoursWorked`. Both should have a `calculatePay()` method. For `SalariedEmployee`, it returns the monthly salary. For `HourlyEmployee`, it's rate times hours. The test should calculate the pay for one of each type."
Basic Class Design,"Digital Music Player","Design `Song` and `Playlist` classes. `Song` has `title`, `artist`, and `duration`. `Playlist` manages a list of `Song` objects. The `Playlist` class should have methods `addSong`, `removeSong`, `getTotalDuration`, `shuffle`, and `playNext`. The `Song` class constructor should not allow an empty title or artist. The `Playlist` should have a `nowPlaying` state. The test should create a playlist, add songs, shuffle it, and play a few tracks."
Basic Class Design,"Elevator Simulator","Create an `Elevator` class with `currentFloor`, `maxFloors`, and `direction` ('UP', 'DOWN', 'IDLE'). Include methods `requestFloor(floor)`, `move()`, and `getDirection()`. The `move` method should change the `currentFloor` by one in the current direction. The logic must handle changing directions when it reaches the top or bottom floor. The test should simulate a few floor requests."
Basic Class Design,"Course and Students","Design a `Student` class with `studentId` and `name`. Design a `Course` class with `courseName` and a list of enrolled `Student` objects. The `Course` class needs methods to `enrollStudent(student)` and `getEnrollmentCount()`. It should not be possible to enroll the same student twice. The test should create a course, enroll several unique students, and attempt to enroll a duplicate."
Basic Class Design,"Time Class","Create a `Time` class with private attributes for `hour`, `minute`, and `second`. The constructor and setters must validate that hour is 0-23, minute is 0-59, and second is 0-59. Include a method `displayStandardTime()` (e.g., '02:30:15 PM') and `displayMilitaryTime()` (e.g., '14:30:15'). Also include an `addSeconds(secs)` method that correctly handles rollover of minutes and hours."
Basic Class Design,"Geometric Shape Calculator","Create an abstract class `Shape` with abstract methods `calculateArea()` and `calculatePerimeter()`. Create concrete subclasses `Circle` (needs radius), `Rectangle` (needs width, height), and `RightTriangle` (needs base, height). Each must implement the abstract methods. The test should create an array of `Shape` objects and print the area and perimeter of each."
Basic Class Design,"User Factory","Create a `User` class with a private constructor. Create a static factory method `createUser(username, password)` inside the `User` class. This factory method should perform validation (e.g., password must be > 8 chars) and only return a `User` object if the data is valid, otherwise return null. The test should use this factory method to create a valid user and attempt to create an invalid one."
Basic Class Design,"Simple ATM Machine","Design `BankAccount` and `ATM` classes. `BankAccount` should be encapsulated with methods for `deposit`, `withdraw`, and `getBalance`, and include a `pin`. The `ATM` class is composed of a `BankAccount` object. The `ATM` has methods like `insertCard(account)`, `enterPin(pin)`, `withdrawCash(amount)`. The `ATM` must manage a session state (e.g., card inserted, pin verified). The test should simulate a user withdrawing cash."
Basic Class Design,"Blog Post with Comments","Design a `Comment` class (`author`, `text`, `timestamp`) and a `BlogPost` class (`title`, `content`, a list of `Comment` objects). The `BlogPost` class should have an `addComment(author, text)` method that creates a new `Comment` object and adds it to the list. The `BlogPost` class should also have a `display()` method that shows the post and all its comments. The test should create a post and add several comments."
Basic Class Design,"Game Character with Inventory","Create a `GameCharacter` class with `name`, `health`, and a list of `Item` objects (where `Item` is another class with `name` and `weight`). The character class should have a `maxWeight` attribute. The `pickupItem(item)` method should only add the item if it doesn't exceed the character's `maxWeight`. Include `takeDamage(amount)` and `heal(amount)` methods that modify health but don't go above `maxHealth` or below 0."
Basic Class Design,"Payment Method System","Create an interface `Payable` with a method `pay(amount)`. Create three classes that implement this interface: `CreditCard`, `PayPal`, and `CryptoWallet`. `CreditCard` needs `cardNumber` and `expiryDate`. `PayPal` needs `email`. `CryptoWallet` needs `walletAddress`. Each `pay` method should print a message specific to the payment type. The test should process a payment with each of the three types."
Basic Class Design,"Age Calculator","Create a `Person` class with private `name` and `birthDate` attributes. The constructor must validate that the birth date is in the past. Include a public method `getAge()` that calculates and returns the person's current age in years based on their birth date and the current date (September 27, 2025). The test should create a person and display their calculated age."
Basic Class Design,"Immutable GPS Coordinate","Design an immutable `Coordinate` class with private final `latitude` and `longitude`. The constructor must validate that latitude is between -90 and 90, and longitude is between -180 and 180. Add a method `distanceTo(otherCoordinate)` that calculates the distance between two points. Since it's immutable, there are no setters. The test should create two valid coordinates and calculate the distance."
Basic Class Design,"Airline Reservation","Design `Passenger`, `Flight`, and `Booking` classes. `Passenger` has `name` and `passportNumber`. `Flight` has `flightNumber`, `destination`, and `capacity`. `Booking` links a `Passenger` to a `Flight` and has a `bookingId`. The `Flight` class must manage its enrollment, not allowing bookings beyond its capacity. The `Booking` class constructor should use a static counter for `bookingId`. The test should create a flight, book several passengers, and handle a case where the flight is full."
Basic Class Design,"String Helper","Create a final class `StringUtils` with a private constructor. Add public static methods like `reverse(String str)`, `isPalindrome(String str)`, and `countVowels(String str)`. The test should call these utility methods directly on the class without creating an instance."
Basic Class Design,"House with Rooms","Design a `Room` class with `name` ('kitchen', 'bedroom', etc.) and `squareFootage`. Design a `House` class that manages a list of `Room` objects. The `House` class should have an `addRoom(room)` method and a `getTotalSquareFootage()` method that sums the square footage of all its rooms. The test should build a house by adding rooms and then calculate the total size."
Basic Class Design,"Product Taxonomy","Create a base class `Product` (`id`, `name`, `price`). Create two derived classes: `Book` and `Electronics`. `Book` adds `author` and `isbn`. `Electronics` adds `brand` and `warrantyPeriod` (in months). Override a `display()` method in each subclass to show its specific details. The test should display the details of both a book and an electronic item."
Basic Class Design,"Smart Thermostat","Create a `Thermostat` class. It should have `targetTemperature`, `currentTemperature`, and `mode` ('HEAT', 'COOL', 'OFF'). Include a method `checkTemperature()` which, depending on the mode, will print messages like 'Starting heater...' if `currentTemperature` is below `targetTemperature` in 'HEAT' mode, or 'Starting AC...' if it's above in 'COOL' mode. The test should set a mode and target, then change the current temperature to trigger the logic."
Basic Class Design,"Secure Password Manager","Create a `PasswordEntry` class with private attributes for `website`, `username`, and `password`. The constructor must validate that the password meets complexity requirements (e.g., >10 chars, has a number, has a special character). Provide a getter for the password that requires a security token (a simple string for this exercise) to be passed as an argument. The test should create a valid entry and try to get the password with correct and incorrect tokens."
Basic Class Design,"Team with Players","Design a `Player` class (`name`, `jerseyNumber`). Design a `Team` class (`teamName`, `city`, and a list of `Player` objects). The `Team` class must have a method `addPlayer(player)` that ensures no two players have the same `jerseyNumber`. The test should build a team, add valid players, and attempt to add a player with a duplicate number."
Basic Class Design,"Car Dealership Inventory","Design `Car` and `Dealership` classes. `Car` is an encapsulated class with validated attributes (`make`, `model`, `year` > 1950, `price` > 0). The `Dealership` class manages a list of `Car` objects. It should have methods `addCarToInventory(car)`, `listInventory()`, and `findCarsByMake(make)`. The `Car` class should use a static counter for a unique `vehicleId`. The test should populate a dealership's inventory and perform a search."
Basic Class Design,"Document Processing","Create an abstract class `Document` with a `content` attribute and an abstract `print()` method. Create `PDFDocument` and `WordDocument` subclasses. `PDFDocument`'s `print()` method should state 'Printing PDF...'. `WordDocument`'s `print()` method should state 'Printing Word document...' and it should also have a `getWordCount()` method. The test should create both document types and call their methods."
Basic Class Design,"Coffee Machine","Design a `CoffeeMachine` class with internal states for `waterLevel`, `beanLevel`, and `groundsContainerFull`. Include a `makeCoffee()` method that checks all three states before 'making' coffee. If successful, it should decrease water/beans and increase grounds. If not, it should report the specific error (e.g., 'Error: Please refill water.'). Include `refillWater()` and `emptyGrounds()` methods. The test should simulate making coffee, running into an issue, fixing it, and trying again."
Basic Class Design,"Fraction Calculator","Create a `Fraction` class with private integer attributes `numerator` and `denominator`. The constructor must not allow a zero denominator. The constructor should also simplify the fraction upon creation (e.g., 2/4 becomes 1/2). Provide public methods `add(Fraction other)` and `multiply(Fraction other)` that return a new `Fraction` object as the result. Include a `toString()` method to display the fraction (e.g., '1/2')."
Basic Class Design,"Playlist and Songs","Design a `Song` class (`title`, `artist`, `durationSeconds`). Design a `Playlist` class that holds a list of `Song` objects. The `Playlist` class should have methods to `addSong`, `removeSong`, `getPlaylistDuration` (formatted as HH:MM:SS), and `findSong(title)`. The test should create a playlist, add several songs, and display the total duration."
Basic Class Design,"Shape and Color","Create a `Color` class with `r`, `g`, `b` values. Create a base class `Shape` that is composed of a `Color` object. Create derived classes `Circle` and `Square`. Add a `describe()` method to the `Shape` class that describes its color, and have the derived classes override it to also include their shape-specific details (e.g., "A red circle with radius 5.0")."
Basic Class Design,"Unit Converter","Create a final `Converter` class with a private constructor. Add public static methods like `celsiusToFahrenheit(double celsius)`, `kilometersToMiles(double km)`, and `litersToGallons(double liters)`. The test should use these methods to perform several conversions without instantiating the class."
Basic Class Design,"Bank Account with Transactions","Enhance the `BankAccount` class to include a list of `Transaction` objects (another class with `amount`, `date`, `type` like 'DEPOSIT' or 'WITHDRAWAL'). Every time a deposit or withdrawal is made, a new `Transaction` object should be created and added to the list. Add a `getStatement()` method that prints the history of all transactions."
Basic Class Design,"E-commerce Order","Design `Product`, `Customer`, and `Order` classes. A `Customer` has a `name` and `address`. An `Order` has an `orderId` (from a static counter), a `Customer` object, a list of `Product` objects, and an `orderDate`. The `Order` class should have a `calculateTotal()` method. The `Customer`'s address setter should validate it's not empty. The test should simulate a customer placing an order for multiple products."
Basic Class Design,"Event Scheduler","Create an `Event` class with private attributes for `eventName`, `startTime`, and `endTime`. The constructor and setters must validate that `endTime` is after `startTime`. Add a method `getDurationInMinutes()`. The test should create a valid event and attempt to create an invalid one."
Basic Class Design,"A Book with Chapters","Design a `Chapter` class (`title`, `pageCount`). Design a `Book` class that has a `title`, `author`, and a list of `Chapter` objects. The `Book` class should have an `addChapter` method and a `getTotalPageCount` method. The test should construct a book by adding chapters and then calculate the total page count."
Basic Class Design,"Graphical User Interface Elements","Create a base class `UIElement` with `width` and `height`. Create derived classes `Button` (`label`) and `TextBox` (`text`). Both should override a `draw()` method. The `Button`'s `draw` method should print information about the button and its label. The `TextBox`'s `draw` method should show info about the text box and its current text."
Basic Class Design,"API Key Manager","Create a class `APIKeys` with a private constructor. Use a private static `Map` or `Dictionary` to store service names and their corresponding API keys (e.g., "GoogleMaps", "key123"). Add a public static method `getKeyForService(String serviceName)` that retrieves a key. Add a static initializer block to populate the keys. The test should retrieve a key for a service."
Basic Class Design,"Simple Text Editor","Create a `TextEditor` class with `text` content and an `undoHistory` (a list of previous text states). The `write(newText)` method should append text and save the *previous* state to the history. The `undo()` method should restore the text to the most recent state from the history. The test should simulate writing text and then undoing an action."
Basic Class Design,"Rental Car System","Design `Car` (encapsulated, validated) and `RentalAgency` classes. `Car` should also have a boolean `isRented` status. The `RentalAgency` manages a list of `Car` objects. It needs methods `rentCar(model)` which finds an available car of that model, marks it as rented, and returns it; and `returnCar(car)` which marks it as not rented. The test should simulate renting and returning a car."
Basic Class Design,"FileSystem Simulation","Design `File` (`name`, `size`) and `Directory` (`name`, a list of `File` objects, and a list of other `Directory` objects) classes. The `Directory` class should have methods to `addFile`, `addDirectory`, and `calculateTotalSize` (which recursively calculates the size of all files and subdirectories). The test should build a small directory tree and calculate its total size."
Basic Class Design,"Time Duration","Create a `Duration` class that internally stores a total number of seconds. Provide a constructor that can take seconds, or minutes and seconds, or hours, minutes, and seconds. Provide getter methods like `getTotalSeconds()`, `getTotalMinutes()`, and `getTotalHours()`. Add a `formatted()` method that returns a string like "01h 30m 15s"."
Basic Class Design,"Employee Types","Create a base `Employee` class. Create derived classes `Manager`, `Engineer`, and `Intern`. `Manager` has a list of subordinate `Employee`s. `Engineer` has a `programmingLanguage`. `Intern` has a `universityName`. All should have a `getDetails()` method that returns a string with their specific information. The test should create one of each type and display their details."
Basic Class Design,"VCR Player","Create a `VCR` class that simulates an old VCR. Have states for `PLAYING`, `PAUSED`, `STOPPED`, `REWINDING` (use an enum). Include methods `play()`, `pause()`, `stop()`, and `rewind()`. Each method can only be called from a valid state (e.g., you can't `pause` if you are `STOPPED`). The test should simulate a sequence of valid and invalid actions."
Basic Class Design,"Quiz Application","Design `Question` and `Quiz` classes. `Question` has a `prompt`, a list of `options`, and the `correctAnswerIndex`. `Quiz` manages a list of `Question` objects and tracks the `userScore`. The `Quiz` class needs methods `start()`, `answerQuestion(questionIndex, userAnswerIndex)`, and `getScore()`. The `Question` constructor should validate that the `correctAnswerIndex` is valid. The test should run a short quiz."
Basic Class Design,"Human Body Composition","Design `Organ` (`name`, `function`) and `Human` (`name`, a list of `Organ` objects) classes. The `Human` class constructor could pre-populate a few essential organs (Heart, Lungs, Brain). Include a method `performFunction(organName)`. The test should create a human and have them use their brain to 'think'."
Basic Class Design,"Domain Name","Create a `DomainName` class that stores a domain as a string. The constructor must validate that the domain follows basic rules (e.g., contains at least one '.', no spaces, valid top-level domain like .com, .org). Add getters like `getTopLevelDomain()` and `getSubdomain()`. The test should create valid and invalid domain names."
Basic Class Design,"Musical Instrument Hierarchy","Create an abstract class `Instrument` with an abstract `playNote(note)` method. Create derived classes `Guitar` (`numberOfStrings`), `Piano` (`numberOfKeys`), and `Trumpet` (`numberOfValves`). Each should implement `playNote` with a custom message. The test should create an orchestra (an array of `Instrument`) and have each instrument play a note."
Basic Class Design,"Email Validator","Create a final `EmailValidator` class with a private constructor. Add a single public static method `isValid(String email)` that returns a boolean. The validation logic should check for an '@' symbol, at least one '.' after the '@', and no spaces. The test should check several valid and invalid email addresses."
Basic Class Design,"Turn-based Game","Create a `Game` class that manages a game between two `Player` objects. The `Game` class should track whose `turn` it is. It needs a `takeTurn(player)` method that only allows the correct player to take a turn and then switches the turn to the other player. The test should simulate a few turns of the game, including an attempt by a player to take a turn out of sequence."
Basic Class Design,"Recipe Book","Design `Ingredient` (`name`, `quantity`, `unit`), `Recipe` (`name`, a list of `Ingredient` objects, `instructions`), and `RecipeBook` (a list of `Recipe` objects) classes. The `RecipeBook` should have `addRecipe` and `findRecipesWithIngredient(ingredientName)` methods. The `Ingredient` constructor should validate that quantity is positive. The test should create a recipe book and search for a recipe."
Basic Class Design,"Solar System","Design a `Planet` class (`name`, `mass`, `distanceFromSun`) and a `SolarSystem` class that has a `starName` and a list of `Planet` objects. The `SolarSystem` class should have a method `getFurthestPlanet()`. The test should create our solar system, add a few planets, and find the one furthest from the sun."
Basic Class Design,"ISBN Validator","Create an `ISBN` class. The constructor takes a 13-digit string. It must validate that the input is exactly 13 characters and consists only of digits. It should also perform the ISBN-13 check-digit validation. Provide a `getFormatted()` method that returns the ISBN with hyphens (e.g., '978-0-306-40615-7')."
Basic Class Design,"Bank Teller and Manager","Create a `BankEmployee` base class. Create derived classes `Teller` and `Manager`. `Teller` has a method `processTransaction(amount)`. `Manager` has a method `approveLoan(amount)` and a list of tellers they manage. The test should create a manager who oversees several tellers."
Basic Class Design,"Subscription Service","Create a `Subscription` class with `serviceName`, `monthlyFee`, and a status (`ACTIVE`, `CANCELLED`, `PAST_DUE`). Include methods `payBill()` (sets status to `ACTIVE`), `missPayment()` (sets status to `PAST_DUE`), and `cancel()` (sets status to `CANCELLED`). The test should walk a subscription through these state changes."
Basic Class Design,"Movie Theater","Design `Movie` (title, duration, rating), `Theater` (theater number, capacity), and `Showtime` (links a `Movie` to a `Theater` at a specific `time`, keeps track of `ticketsSold`) classes. The `Showtime` class should have a `sellTicket()` method that fails if capacity is reached. `Movie` rating should be a validated enum (G, PG, PG-13, R). The test should create a movie, schedule a showtime, and sell tickets."
Basic Class Design,"Personal Computer with Peripherals","Design `Peripheral` (`type` like 'Mouse' or 'Keyboard', `brand`). Design a `PC` class that is composed of a `CPU`, `RAM`, and a list of `Peripheral` objects. The `PC` class should have `addPeripheral` and `listPeripherals` methods. The test should build a PC and add a mouse and keyboard."
Basic Class Design,"Geographic Location","Create a `GeoLocation` class. The constructor should accept latitude and longitude and validate them. Include a method `getQuadrant()` that returns a string like 'North-West', 'South-East', etc., based on the signs of the latitude and longitude. The test should create locations in all four quadrants."
Basic Class Design,"Vehicle Rental","Create a base `RentalVehicle` class (`make`, `model`, `rentalRate`). Create derived classes `Car` (`passengerCapacity`) and `Truck` (`cargoCapacityInTons`). Override a `calculateRentalFee(days)` method in each subclass, where Trucks might have an additional mileage charge. The test should calculate the rental fee for a car and a truck for 5 days."
Basic Class Design,"Application Logger","Design a `Logger` class (using the Singleton pattern) that can log messages with different severity levels (use an enum: `INFO`, `WARN`, `ERROR`). It should have a static method `log(level, message)` that prepends the timestamp and severity to the message before printing it. The test should log one message of each severity level."
Basic Class Design,"Smart Light Bulb","Create a `SmartBulb` class. It should have attributes for `isOn` (boolean), `brightness` (0-100), and `color` (an `RGBColor` object). Include methods `turnOn()`, `turnOff()`, `setBrightness(level)`, and `setColor(r, g, b)`. The `setBrightness` method should only work if the bulb `isOn`. The test should simulate turning on the bulb and adjusting its settings."
Basic Class Design,"Pet Store Inventory","Design a `Pet` abstract class with a `speak()` method. Create concrete pets like `Dog` and `Cat`. The `PetStore` class manages a list of `Pet` objects for sale. Each pet has a price. The `PetStore` has methods to `addPet` and `sellPet`. The `Pet`'s constructor should use a static counter for a unique pet ID. The `PetStore` should track total revenue. The test should stock the store, sell a pet, and check the revenue."
Basic Class Design,"Meal and Ingredients","Design an `Ingredient` class (`name`, `calories`). Design a `Meal` class that has a `name` ('Breakfast', 'Lunch', etc.) and a list of `Ingredient` objects. The `Meal` class should have a `calculateTotalCalories()` method. The test should create a meal, add ingredients, and calculate the total calories."
Basic Class Design,"Conference Room Booking","Create a `ConferenceRoom` class (`roomName`, `capacity`). Create a `Booking` class with a `ConferenceRoom`, a `startTime`, and an `endTime`. The constructor for `Booking` must validate that the end time is after the start time. The test should create a valid booking."
Basic Class Design,"Wizarding World Characters","Create a base `MagicalBeing` class. Create derived classes `Wizard` and `HouseElf`. A `Wizard` has a `wand` (a `Wand` object) and can `castSpell()`. A `HouseElf` has a `familyName` it serves and can `performMagic()` without a wand. The test should create a wizard and a house-elf and demonstrate their unique abilities."
Basic Class Design,"Web Browser Tab","Create a `BrowserTab` class with a `currentURL` and a `history` (a list of visited URLs). Include a `MapsTo(url)` method that updates the `currentURL` and adds the *previous* URL to the history. Include `back()` and `forward()` methods that navigate through the history (this requires tracking the current position in the history list)."
Basic Class Design,"Auction System","Design `AuctionItem` (encapsulated `name`, `startingPrice`), `Bid` (`bidderName`, `amount`), and `Auction` classes. The `Auction` class manages one `AuctionItem` and a list of `Bid` objects. It needs a `placeBid(bidderName, amount)` method that only accepts a bid if it's higher than the current highest bid. It should also have a `getWinningBid()` method. Use a static counter for `AuctionItem` IDs. The test should simulate a simple auction."
Basic Class Design,"Online Order Fulfillment","Design an `Order` class managing a list of `Product`s. The `Order` must have a status (enum: `PENDING`, `PROCESSING`, `SHIPPED`, `DELIVERED`). Create methods `processOrder()`, `shipOrder()`, and `deliverOrder()` that can only be called in the correct sequence. Each method updates the status. The test should simulate a valid order lifecycle and an invalid one (e.g., trying to deliver a processing order)."
Basic Class Design,"University Personnel System","Create an abstract `Person` class with `name`. Create `Student` and `Professor` classes inheriting from `Person`. `Student` has a `major`. `Professor` has a `specialty`. Now, create a `Department` class composed of one `Professor` (the chair) and a list of other `Professor`s. The test should build a department and display its roster."
Basic Class Design,"Validated Financial Transaction Factory","Create a `Transaction` class with private `id`, `amount`, and `timestamp`. The constructor must be private. Create a public static factory method `createTransaction(amount)` that validates the amount is positive. If valid, it should create a new `Transaction`, assign it a unique ID from a static counter, and set the current timestamp. If invalid, it returns null. The test should use the factory to create valid and invalid transactions."
Basic Class Design,"Photo Album","Design `Photo` (`filename`, `dateTaken`) and `PhotoAlbum` (`albumTitle`) classes. The `PhotoAlbum` must manage a list of `Photo` objects. It needs methods to `addPhoto`, `removePhoto`, and `getPhotosTakenOn(date)`. The `addPhoto` method should prevent duplicate filenames. The test should create an album, add photos, and find all photos from a specific date."
Basic Class Design,"Zoo Enclosure Management","Create an abstract `Animal` class with properties `species` and `foodType`. It must have an abstract method `makeSound()`. Create concrete `Mammal`, `Bird`, and `Reptile` classes that inherit from `Animal`. Create an `Enclosure` class that can hold a list of `Animal`s but has a rule that only animals of the same type (e.g., all Mammals) can be in the same enclosure. The test should enforce this rule."
Basic Class Design,"Task Management System","Create a `Task` class with `description` and a status (enum: `TODO`, `IN_PROGRESS`, `DONE`). It should also have `assignee` and `dueDate` attributes. The constructor must validate that the due date is in the future. Methods `startTask()` and `completeTask()` transition the state. A task cannot be started if it's already done. The test should manage a task's lifecycle."
Basic Class Design,"Ecosystem Simulation","Design `Plant` and `Herbivore` classes. A `Plant` has `calories`. An `Herbivore` has an `energyLevel` and an `eat(Plant)` method that increases its energy. Now, create an `Ecosystem` class that manages lists of `Plant`s and `Herbivore`s. The `Ecosystem` should have a `simulateDay()` method where herbivores with low energy will eat a random plant. The test should simulate a few days in the ecosystem."
Basic Class Design,"Secure API Key","Create an `ApiKey` class that stores a `key` string privately. The constructor must validate that the key is exactly 32 alphanumeric characters. Include a method `isValid()` that re-checks this rule. Also, include a `getMaskedKey()` method that returns the key with the first 28 characters masked (e.g., 'XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX1234')."
Basic Class Design,"GUI Element Rendering","Create an abstract `UIComponent` class with an abstract `render()` method. Create concrete subclasses `Button` (`label`), `TextField` (`value`), and `Checkbox` (`isChecked`). Each should implement `render()` to print an HTML-like representation (e.g., `<button>Click Me</button>`). The test should create a list of `UIComponent`s and render them all in a loop."
Basic Class Design,"Smart Home Hub","Design a `SmartHomeHub` (Singleton). Create an abstract `Device` class with `turnOn()` and `turnOff()` methods. Create `SmartLight` (with `brightness`) and `Thermostat` (with `temperature`) subclasses. The `SmartHomeHub` should manage a list of `Device`s. It needs a `turnEverythingOff()` method that iterates through all devices and turns them off. The test should set up a home with devices and trigger this method."
Basic Class Design,"Molecule Builder","Design an `Atom` class with `elementName` (e.g., 'Carbon') and `atomicWeight`. Design a `Molecule` class with a `commonName` (e.g., 'Water') and a list of `Atom` objects. The `Molecule` class needs a `calculateMolecularWeight()` method that sums the atomic weights of all its atoms. The test should build a water molecule (H2O) and calculate its weight."
Basic Class Design,"Vending Machine Change","Enhance a `VendingMachine` class to manage change. It should have attributes for the number of quarters, dimes, and nickels it holds. When a user makes a purchase and is owed change, the `dispenseChange()` method must calculate and return the correct number of each coin, updating its internal coin counts. The logic must handle cases where exact change cannot be made."
Basic Class Design,"Question Types for a Quiz","Create a base `Question` class with a `prompt` and an abstract `isCorrect(answer)` method. Create derived classes `MultipleChoiceQuestion` (has a list of options and a correct index) and `TextQuestion` (has a correct answer string, should be case-insensitive). The test should create a quiz with a list containing both types of questions and check answers for each."
Basic Class Design,"Immutable Date Range","Create an immutable `DateRange` class with private final `startDate` and `endDate` attributes. The constructor must validate that `startDate` is before `endDate`. Include methods like `getDurationInDays()` and `overlaps(otherRange)` which returns true if the two date ranges have any overlap. The test should check for overlaps between different date ranges."
Basic Class Design,"Company and Employees","Create an `Employee` class with a unique `employeeId` (generated by a static counter), `name`, and `salary`. Create a `Company` class that manages a list of `Employee` objects. The `Company` class should have methods to `hireEmployee(name, salary)`, `fireEmployee(employeeId)`, and `calculateTotalPayroll()` which is the sum of all employee salaries."
Basic Class Design,"Musical Instrument Tuner","Create an abstract `Instrument` class with an abstract `tune()` method and a `isTuned` boolean property. Create concrete classes `Guitar` (which tunes by adjusting strings) and `Piano` (which tunes by adjusting keys). The `tune()` method in each should set `isTuned` to true. Create a `Tuner` class with a static method `tuneInstrument(Instrument inst)` that calls the instrument's tune method."
Basic Class Design,"Subscription Model","Design a `User` class with a `Subscription` object. The `Subscription` has a status (enum: `FREE_TRIAL`, `ACTIVE`, `CANCELED`). Include methods `upgradeToPaid()` (changes from `FREE_TRIAL` to `ACTIVE`) and `cancel()`. A user on a free trial cannot access `premiumFeature()`, but an active subscriber can. The test should check access control based on subscription state."
Basic Class Design,"Car with Wheels and Engine","Design `Wheel` (`position`), `Engine` (`horsepower`), and `Car` classes. A `Car` must be composed of exactly one `Engine` and four `Wheel` objects (e.g., 'Front-Left', 'Front-Right', etc.). The `Car`'s constructor should require these components. Include a `drive()` method that conceptually checks if all components are present before driving."
Basic Class Design,"Player Character Classes","Create a base `PlayerCharacter` class with `name` and `health`. Create derived classes `Warrior` (with `rage` attribute), `Mage` (with `mana` attribute), and `Rogue` (with `energy` attribute). Each class should have a unique `specialAbility()` method that uses its specific resource (rage, mana, or energy)."
Basic Class Design,"Investment Portfolio","Create a `Stock` class with `tickerSymbol` and `sharePrice`. The setter for `sharePrice` must ensure it's not negative. Create a `Portfolio` class that manages a list of `Stock`s. The `Portfolio` needs a `getTotalValue()` method and a `getPortfolioDiversity()` method that returns the number of unique stocks."
Basic Class Design,"Flight Manifest","Design `Passenger` (encapsulated) and `Flight` classes. The `Flight` class manages a list of `Passenger` objects and has a `seatCapacity`. The `addPassenger(passenger)` method must not exceed the `seatCapacity`. The `Flight` class should also have a `getManifest()` method that returns a formatted list of all passengers. A `Passenger` should have a validated passport number."
Basic Class Design,"Multi-stage Rocket","Design a `Rocket` class that is composed of a list of `Stage` objects. Each `Stage` has `fuel` and a boolean `isIgnited`. The `Rocket` has a `launch()` method that ignites the first stage. It also has a `separateStage()` method that discards the current stage and ignites the next one, but only if the current stage has run out of fuel."
Basic Class Design,"A Recipe with Instructions","Design an `Ingredient` class (`name`, `amount`). Design a `Recipe` class that holds a list of `Ingredient`s and a list of `Instruction` strings. Include a `scaleRecipe(factor)` method that creates and returns a *new* `Recipe` object with all ingredient amounts multiplied by the factor. The test should create a recipe and scale it up."
Basic Class Design,"Bank Account Fees","Create an abstract `BankAccount` with `balance`. Create a concrete `CheckingAccount` and `SavingsAccount`. The abstract class should have an abstract `applyMonthlyFees()` method. The `CheckingAccount` might charge a flat fee if the balance is low. The `SavingsAccount` might charge no fees but give interest. The test should apply fees to both account types."
Basic Class Design,"Date Formatting Utility","Create a final `DateUtils` class with a private constructor. Add public static methods like `formatAsMDY(date)` which returns a string like '09/27/2025' and `isWeekend(date)` which returns a boolean. The test should use these methods on the current date."
Basic Class Design,"Rental Property Manager","Design `Tenant` (encapsulated `name`, `creditScore`), `RentalProperty` (`address`, `monthlyRent`), and `PropertyManager` classes. The `PropertyManager` manages a list of `RentalProperty` objects. A property can have one `Tenant`. The manager needs methods `rentProperty(address, tenant)` (which checks the tenant's credit score is above a threshold) and `collectRent()` which iterates through all rented properties."
Basic Class Design,"Immutable GPS Path","Create an immutable `GPSPoint` class. Create a `Path` class that manages a list of `GPSPoint` objects. The `Path` class should be immutable as well: its constructor takes the list of points, and any methods like `addPoint(point)` must return a *new* `Path` object with the added point, rather than modifying the existing one. Include a `calculateTotalDistance()` method."
Basic Class Design,"Software Build Pipeline","Create a `Build` class with a status (enum: `QUEUED`, `COMPILING`, `TESTING`, `FAILED`, `SUCCESSFUL`). Create a `Pipeline` class that manages a queue of `Build`s. The `Pipeline`'s `run()` method processes one build at a time, transitioning it through the states (conceptually, with print statements). A failure in the `TESTING` state should move it to `FAILED`."
Basic Class Design,"Art Gallery","Create an abstract `Artwork` class (`artist`, `year`). Create derived classes `Painting` (`medium`) and `Sculpture` (`material`). Create a `Gallery` class that is composed of a list of `Artwork` objects. The gallery needs a method `getArtworksByArtist(artistName)`. The test should populate a gallery and search for works by a specific artist."
Basic Class Design,"A Deck of Cards","Design a `Card` class (`suit`, `rank`). Design a `Deck` class whose constructor creates the standard 52 `Card` objects and holds them in a list. The `Deck` needs a `shuffle()` method that randomizes the list and a `dealOne()` method that removes and returns the top card from the deck. The test should shuffle a deck and deal a few cards."
Basic Class Design,"Simple CRM","Design `Contact` (encapsulated, validated email) and `Interaction` (`date`, `notes`) classes. Design a `CRM` class that manages a list of `Contact`s. Each `Contact` object in the CRM should also have its own list of `Interaction`s. The `CRM` needs a method `addInteraction(contactEmail, notes)` that finds the right contact and adds a new interaction to their history."
Basic Class Design,"Traffic Intersection","Design an `Intersection` class that manages two `TrafficLight` objects (one for North-South, one for East-West). When one light is Green, the other must be Red. The `cycle()` method of the `Intersection` should manage the entire state change sequence for both lights (e.g., NS Green -> NS Yellow -> NS Red & EW Green, etc.)."
Basic Class Design,"Fantasy Character Inventory","Create a base `Item` class (`name`, `weight`). Create derived classes `Weapon` (`damage`), `Armor` (`defense`), and `Potion` (`healingAmount`). Create a `Character` class with an `Inventory` that can hold a list of `Item`s. The `Inventory` should have a `getTotalWeight()` method. The test should add various items to the inventory and check the weight."
Basic Class Design,"Global Meeting Scheduler","Create a `Meeting` class with a `topic` and a `utcTimestamp`. Include a method `getLocalTime(timezone)` that takes a timezone string (e.g., 'America/New_York') and returns the meeting time as a formatted string for that zone. The test should schedule a meeting in UTC and display its time for New York, London, and Tokyo."
Basic Class Design,"Computer with Operating System","Design an `OperatingSystem` class (`name`, `version`). Design a `Computer` class that is composed of a `CPU`, `RAM`, and an `OperatingSystem` object. The `Computer` needs a `boot()` method that prints information about the OS starting up. The test should create a computer running a specific OS."
Basic Class Design,"Employee Workflows","Create an abstract `Employee` class with an abstract `doWork()` method. Create concrete `Developer` (`favoriteLanguage`), `Designer` (`favoriteSoftware`), and `Manager` (`teamSize`) classes. Each should implement `doWork()` with a message specific to their role. Create a `Company` class that has a list of `Employee`s and a `startWorkday()` method that calls `doWork()` on every employee."
Basic Class Design,"Smart TV","Design a `SmartTV` class with attributes `isOn`, `currentChannel`, and `currentApp` (e.g., 'Netflix'). It can only be on one app or one channel at a time. Create methods `switchToChannel(channelNum)` and `launchApp(appName)`. Launching an app should set the channel to null, and vice-versa. The test should simulate switching between TV channels and apps."
Basic Class Design,"Public Library Loan System","Design `Book` (with an `isAvailable` status), `Patron` (with a list of currently borrowed `Book`s), and `Library` classes. The `Library` manages the master list of all its `Book`s and a list of registered `Patron`s. It needs a `loanBook(patronId, bookIsbn)` method that checks if the book is available and the patron's loan limit is not exceeded, then updates the states of the book and patron. A `returnBook` method is also needed."
Basic Class Design,"Secure Document","Create a `SecureDocument` class with private `content` and a private `password`. The constructor sets both. Include a `getContent(providedPassword)` method that only returns the content if the provided password is correct, otherwise it returns an error message. There should be no direct getter for the password."
Basic Class Design,"A Zoo with Enclosures","Design an `Animal` class. Design an `Enclosure` class (`habitatType`, a list of `Animal`s). Design a `Zoo` class that manages a list of `Enclosure`s. The `Zoo` class should have a method `findAnimal(species)` that searches through all enclosures to find an animal. The test should build a zoo with several enclosures and animals, then find one."
Basic Class Design,"Subscription Tiers","Create a base `Subscription` class with `price`. Create derived classes `Basic`, `Premium`, and `Family`. `Basic` has a `deviceLimit` of 1. `Premium` has a `deviceLimit` of 5 and supports `HD` streaming. `Family` has a `profileLimit`. Override a `displayFeatures()` method in each tier. The test should create and display the features of a `Premium` subscription."
Basic Class Design,"Currency Formatting Utility","Create a final `CurrencyUtils` class with a private constructor. Add a public static method `format(amount, currencyCode)` that takes a double and a string (e.g., "USD", "EUR", "JPY") and returns a properly formatted currency string (e.g., "$1,234.56", "€1.234,56"). The test should format amounts in several different currencies."
Basic Class Design,"E-Reader Device","Design an `EBook` class (`title`, `content`). Design an `EReader` class that holds a library (list of `EBook`s) and tracks the `currentPage` of the `currentlyReading` `EBook`. Include methods `openBook(book)`, `nextPage()`, `previousPage()`, and `closeBook()`. The `nextPage` method should not go past the end of the book."
Basic Class Design,"University Course Catalog","Design `Professor` (encapsulated), `Course` (composed of a `Professor`), and `CourseCatalog` classes. The `CourseCatalog` manages a list of all available `Course`s. It needs methods to `addCourse`, `findCoursesByProfessor(profName)`, and `findCoursesByDepartment(deptCode)`. The `Course` ID should be a validated string like 'CS-101'. The test should populate a catalog and perform searches."
Basic Class Design,"A Car with a Trip Computer","Design a `TripComputer` class that tracks `milesDriven`, `fuelConsumed`, and can calculate `milesPerGallon`. Design a `Car` class that is composed of an `Engine` and a `TripComputer`. The `Car`'s `drive(miles, fuel)` method should update the `TripComputer`. The test should simulate a trip and then get the MPG from the trip computer."
Basic Class Design,"Appointment Scheduler","Create an `Appointment` class with private `clientName`, `dateTime`, and `durationInMinutes`. The constructor must validate that the appointment time is during business hours (e.g., 9 AM to 5 PM). Create an `AppointmentBook` class that manages a list of `Appointment`s and has an `addAppointment` method that ensures no two appointments overlap."
Basic Class Design,"Spacecraft Types","Create an abstract `Spacecraft` class with an abstract `launch()` method. Create derived classes `Satellite` (has a `purpose`, like 'GPS'), `Probe` (has a `destination`, like 'Mars'), and `Shuttle` (has `crewCapacity`). Each should implement `launch` with a custom message. The test should launch one of each type."
Basic Class Design,"Multi-player Game Lobby","Design a `Player` class. Design a `GameLobby` class that manages a list of `Player`s and has a status (`WAITING`, `COUNTDOWN`, `IN_GAME`). The lobby has a `minPlayers` and `maxPlayers` count. The `addPlayer` method works only in the `WAITING` state. When `minPlayers` is reached, the status changes to `COUNTDOWN`. The test should simulate players joining and the lobby status changing."
Basic Class Design,"Bank with Customers and Accounts","Design `Customer` (encapsulated, static ID), `Account` (abstract), and `Bank` classes. The `Bank` manages a list of `Customer`s. Each `Customer` can have a list of `Account`s (`Checking`, `Savings`). The `Bank` needs a method `getCustomerTotalBalance(customerId)` that finds a customer and sums the balances of all their accounts."
Basic Class Design,"A Pizza with Toppings","Design an `Ingredient` class (`name`, `price`). Design a `Pizza` class that has a `basePrice` and a list of `Ingredient` objects (toppings). The `Pizza` class needs a `calculateTotalPrice()` method that adds the price of all toppings to the base price. The test should build a custom pizza and calculate its final price."
Basic Class Design,"Immutable Time Period","Create an immutable `TimePeriod` class that represents a duration. The constructor should accept a number of days, hours, and minutes and store the total duration internally in seconds. It must validate that all inputs are non-negative. Provide getters like `getTotalHours()` and `getAsMinutes()`. There should be no setters."
Basic Class Design,"Computer File System","Create a base `FileSystemEntity` class with `name` and `dateCreated`. Create derived classes `File` (`sizeInBytes`) and `Directory` (a list of `FileSystemEntity` objects). The `Directory` class should have a `getTotalSize()` method that recursively calculates its total size. The test should build a small directory structure and calculate its size."
Basic Class Design,"Password Strength Checker","Create a final `PasswordChecker` class with a private constructor. Add a public static method `checkStrength(password)` that returns an enum (`WEAK`, `MEDIUM`, `STRONG`). The logic should check for length, presence of uppercase letters, numbers, and special characters. The test should check one of each type of password."
Basic Class Design,"Microwave with Cooking Modes","Design a `Microwave` class with states (`IDLE`, `COOKING`, `DOOR_OPEN`). It should also have cooking modes (`POPCORN`, `DEFROST`, `MANUAL`). The `start(mode, time)` method only works from the `IDLE` state and sets the mode. The `openDoor()` method should pause cooking if it's in the `COOKING` state. The test should simulate these interactions."
Basic Class Design,"Social Media Post","Design `Comment` (encapsulated), `User` (static ID), and `Post` classes. A `Post` is created by a `User` and has `content` and a list of `Comment`s. Each `Comment` is also associated with a `User`. The `Post` class needs a `like(User)` method that adds a user to a list of 'likers' and prevents a user from liking a post more than once."
Basic Class Design,"A Human with a Brain and Heart","Design `Brain` (`iq`) and `Heart` (`bpm`) classes. Design a `Human` class whose constructor requires a `Brain` and a `Heart` object. The `Human`'s `live()` method should print messages conceptually using its brain ('Thinking...') and heart ('Pumping...'). The test should create a human with these composed parts."
Basic Class Design,"Color Mixer","Create an `RGBColor` class (validated 0-255). Include a non-static `mix(RGBColor other)` method that takes another color, averages the R, G, and B values, and returns a *new* `RGBColor` object representing the mixture. The test should mix two colors to create a third."
Basic Class Design,"E-commerce Product Variations","Create a base `Product` class. Create a derived `Apparel` class which adds `size` and `color`. The `Apparel` constructor should take a base product and the variation data. This allows you to have a single 'T-Shirt' product with multiple `Apparel` objects representing its variations. The test should create a t-shirt in several sizes and colors."
Basic Class Design,"Stopwatch with Laps","Enhance a `Stopwatch` class. It needs states (`STOPPED`, `RUNNING`). The `start()` and `stop()` methods manage these states. Add a `lap()` method that, only when running, records the current elapsed time into a list of lap times without stopping the main timer. The test should run a stopwatch and record a few laps."
Basic Class Design,"Restaurant Reservation System","Design `Table` (table number, capacity), `Reservation` (customer name, time, `Table` object), and `Restaurant` classes. The `Restaurant` manages a list of `Table`s and a list of `Reservation`s. It needs a `makeReservation(customerName, partySize, time)` method that finds an available table of the right capacity for that time and creates a reservation. The test should handle successful bookings and cases where no tables are available."
Basic Class Design,"A Graphic Document with Layers","Design a `Layer` class (`name`, `isVisible`, `content`). Design a `Document` class that manages an ordered list of `Layer` objects. The `Document` needs methods to `addLayer`, `removeLayer`, and `reorderLayer(fromIndex, toIndex)`. The test should build a document with several layers."
Basic Class Design,"Warranty Tracker","Create a `Product` class with `purchaseDate`. Create a `Warranty` class with a `durationInMonths`. The `Product` should be composed of a `Warranty` object. The `Product` class needs an `isUnderWarranty()` method that checks if the current date (September 27, 2025) is within the warranty period based on the purchase date."
Basic Class Design,"Game Entity AI","Create an abstract `GameEntity` class with `position` and an abstract `update()` method. Create derived classes `Player` (whose `update` method reads user input), `Enemy` (whose `update` method moves towards the player), and `NPC` (whose `update` method stands still and says a phrase). The test should create a list of entities and call `update` on all of them."
Basic Class Design,"File System Helper","Create a final `FileUtils` class with a private constructor. Add public static methods like `getExtension(filename)` which returns the file's extension, and `getFilenameWithoutExtension(filename)`. The test should use these methods on various filenames."
Basic Class Design,"Email Client","Design an `Email` class (`sender`, `subject`, `body`). Design an `EmailClient` class that manages lists of emails for `inbox`, `sent`, and `trash`. It needs methods `sendEmail(email)` (adds to sent), `receiveEmail(email)` (adds to inbox), and `deleteEmail(email)` (moves from inbox to trash). The test should simulate a full email lifecycle."
Basic Class Design,"Genetics Simulator","Design `Gene` (`trait`, `isDominant`) and `Chromosome` (`a list of `Gene`s) classes. Design a `Creature` class composed of a list of `Chromosome` pairs. Write a method `getPhenotype(trait)` that checks the creature's chromosomes to determine if a dominant gene for that trait is present. The test should create a simple creature and check for a specific trait."
Basic Class Design,"A House with an Address","Design an `Address` class (`street`, `city`, `zipCode`). Design a `House` class that is composed of an `Address` object and has other attributes like `squareFootage`. The constructor for `House` should require an `Address` object. The test should create a house at a specific address."
Basic Class Design,"Conference Session Scheduler","Create a `Session` class with `title`, `speaker`, `startTime`, and `duration`. The constructor must validate that the duration is a standard length (e.g., 30, 45, or 60 minutes). Create a `Track` class that manages a list of `Session`s and has an `addSession` method that ensures no two sessions on that track overlap in time."
Basic Class Design,"Role-Playing Game Character Stats","Create a base `Character` class. Create a `Stats` class (`strength`, `dexterity`, `intelligence`). The `Character` class is composed of a `Stats` object. Now, create derived `Warrior` and `Mage` classes. The `Warrior`'s constructor should favor `strength`, while the `Mage`'s should favor `intelligence`, setting these as default values in their `Stats` object."
Basic Class Design,"Air Conditioner Unit","Design an `ACUnit` class with `temperature`, `fanSpeed` (enum: `LOW`, `MEDIUM`, `HIGH`), and `mode` (enum: `COOL`, `FAN_ONLY`). Include methods to change the settings. The `setTemperature` method should only be effective when the mode is `COOL`. The test should simulate changing modes and settings."
Basic Class Design,"Digital Library Card","Design `Patron` (with a static unique `cardId`) and `LibraryCard` classes. A `LibraryCard` is composed of a `Patron` object and has an `expirationDate`. The `LibraryCard` class should have an `isExpired()` method that checks against the current date (September 27, 2025). The test should create a patron, issue them a card, and check if it's expired."
Basic Class Design,"Movie Theater","Design `Movie` (title, duration, rating), `Theater` (theater number, capacity), and `Showtime` (links a `Movie` to a `Theater` at a specific `time`, keeps track of `ticketsSold`) classes. The `Showtime` class should have a `sellTicket()` method that fails if capacity is reached. `Movie` rating should be a validated enum (G, PG, PG-13, R). The test should create a movie, schedule a showtime, and sell tickets."
Basic Class Design,"Personal Computer with Peripherals","Design `Peripheral` (`type` like 'Mouse' or 'Keyboard', `brand`). Design a `PC` class that is composed of a `CPU`, `RAM`, and a list of `Peripheral` objects. The `PC` class should have `addPeripheral` and `listPeripherals` methods. The test should build a PC and add a mouse and keyboard."
Basic Class Design,"Geographic Location","Create a `GeoLocation` class. The constructor should accept latitude and longitude and validate them. Include a method `getQuadrant()` that returns a string like 'North-West', 'South-East', etc., based on the signs of the latitude and longitude. The test should create locations in all four quadrants."
Basic Class Design,"Vehicle Rental","Create a base `RentalVehicle` class (`make`, `model`, `rentalRate`). Create derived classes `Car` (`passengerCapacity`) and `Truck` (`cargoCapacityInTons`). Override a `calculateRentalFee(days)` method in each subclass, where Trucks might have an additional mileage charge. The test should calculate the rental fee for a car and a truck for 5 days."
Basic Class Design,"Application Logger","Design a `Logger` class (using the Singleton pattern) that can log messages with different severity levels (use an enum: `INFO`, `WARN`, `ERROR`). It should have a static method `log(level, message)` that prepends the timestamp and severity to the message before printing it. The test should log one message of each severity level."
Basic Class Design,"Smart Light Bulb","Create a `SmartBulb` class. It should have attributes for `isOn` (boolean), `brightness` (0-100), and `color` (an `RGBColor` object). Include methods `turnOn()`, `turnOff()`, `setBrightness(level)`, and `setColor(r, g, b)`. The `setBrightness` method should only work if the bulb `isOn`. The test should simulate turning on the bulb and adjusting its settings."
Basic Class Design,"Pet Store Inventory","Design a `Pet` abstract class with a `speak()` method. Create concrete pets like `Dog` and `Cat`. The `PetStore` class manages a list of `Pet` objects for sale. Each pet has a price. The `PetStore` has methods to `addPet` and `sellPet`. The `Pet`'s constructor should use a static counter for a unique pet ID. The `PetStore` should track total revenue. The test should stock the store, sell a pet, and check the revenue."
Basic Class Design,"Meal and Ingredients","Design an `Ingredient` class (`name`, `calories`). Design a `Meal` class that has a `name` ('Breakfast', 'Lunch', etc.) and a list of `Ingredient` objects. The `Meal` class should have a `calculateTotalCalories()` method. The test should create a meal, add ingredients, and calculate the total calories."
Basic Class Design,"Conference Room Booking","Create a `ConferenceRoom` class (`roomName`, `capacity`). Create a `Booking` class with a `ConferenceRoom`, a `startTime`, and an `endTime`. The constructor for `Booking` must validate that the end time is after the start time. The test should create a valid booking."
Basic Class Design,"Wizarding World Characters","Create a base `MagicalBeing` class. Create derived classes `Wizard` and `HouseElf`. A `Wizard` has a `wand` (a `Wand` object) and can `castSpell()`. A `HouseElf` has a `familyName` it serves and can `performMagic()` without a wand. The test should create a wizard and a house-elf and demonstrate their unique abilities."
Basic Class Design,"Web Browser Tab","Create a `BrowserTab` class with a `currentURL` and a `history` (a list of visited URLs). Include a `MapsTo(url)` method that updates the `currentURL` and adds the *previous* URL to the history. Include `back()` and `forward()` methods that navigate through the history (this requires tracking the current position in the history list)."
Basic Class Design,"Auction System","Design `AuctionItem` (encapsulated `name`, `startingPrice`), `Bid` (`bidderName`, `amount`), and `Auction` classes. The `Auction` class manages one `AuctionItem` and a list of `Bid` objects. It needs a `placeBid(bidderName, amount)` method that only accepts a bid if it's higher than the current highest bid. It should also have a `getWinningBid()` method. Use a static counter for `AuctionItem` IDs. The test should simulate a simple auction."
